{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms","id":1282574,"title":"Evocations vs Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-24T21:03:02-08:00","id":1282574,"title":"Evocations vs Charms","content":"So, the devs have said that evocations are supposed to extend beyond what native charms can do, but on the other hand evocations need to fit the themes of an artifact's magical material, and the themes of each magical material are extremely close to those of the exalted that are encouraged to use that material the most. How does one distinguish which effects to make charms for a type of exalted and which to make evocations of an artifact of their corresponding magical material?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T22:29:13-08:00","id":1282588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rj.au</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms#post1282574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the devs have said that evocations are supposed to extend beyond what native charms can do, but on the other hand evocations need to fit the themes of an artifact's magical material,</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say to stop there and question that assumption. The themes of each magical material are <i>one source</i> of evocations, but <i>not</i> the only one. An artifact's history and general nature are both just as important sources for evocation ideas. For example, check out the Frost-Thorn Knuckles in Arms of the Chosen. They're moonsilver, but a lot of their evocations are based around ice and general survival in cold climates, neither of which are really noted as moonsilver themes. But they work, because of the artifact's nature and history, which involve magical ice and hunting in arctic terrain, and the Frost-Thorn Knuckles themselves make sense as moonsilver because they were crafted by a Lunar, and have strong animalistic affinities, even if they don't particularly express that in their evocations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the themes of each magical material are extremely close to those of the exalted that are encouraged to use that material the most. </div> </div> </div>And that's the other assumption I'd challenge. The magical materials certainly have overlaps with the Exalted types who resonate with them. But I would disagree that they're &quot;extremely close&quot;. Take orichalcum, for example - while several of its affinities certainly mimic Solar tricks, others don't. It lists &quot;light and <i>shadow</i>&quot;, for example (emphasis mine). Light is certainly within the Solars' wheelhouse, but shadow isn't so much. At best, Night castes with Stealth can hide in shadow. But they probably couldn't create an effect that created shadows, whereas I could totally see an orichalcum lamp that could either brightly illuminate a room, or absorb all light into itself, plunging the whole area into darkness. Or could create animated shadow-puppets! And orichalcum mentions being able to &quot;harness forceful, vibrant, or energetic natural phenomena&quot;, which is generally going to be outside the Solar charmset, I'd say. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does one distinguish which effects to make charms for a type of exalted and which to make evocations of an artifact of their corresponding magical material? </div> </div> </div>As I referred to above, I'd start with the places that the affinity list <i>doesn't</i> overlap with the Exalted's themes, which I think occurs in all of the magical materials. Also, don't be afraid to explore &quot;like the Exalt type in question, but <i>even better</i>&quot; - a Solar can be a deadly swordswoman with any blade she picks up, but a <i>particularly</i> dangerous one with her cherished daiklave that she treats as an extension of her soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T02:58:55-08:00","id":1282607,"title":"","content":"&quot;Like the Exalt type in question, but <i>even better</i>&quot; can especially be true of Jade. Resonant effects are supposed to be close to solar tier, so Jade weapons are a big source of a dragon blooded's strongest powers. Orichalcum too, since solars can use everything equally well and there needs to be some incentive for them to use Orichalcum, because it is true that by using your own material, you sacrifice some of that extension of themes for power. For most exalts, it a bit of a trade off. <br /> <br /> That might be why starmetal is one of the more versatile of the materials, now I think about it, since sidereals are crippled more by branching out than other exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T05:13:32-08:00","id":1282619,"title":"","content":"One factor to keep in mind with regard to the question of whether a particular effect should be a Charm or an Evocation is, &quot;does it make sense for the Exalt to be using it <i>without</i> the Artifact?&quot; <br /> <br /> If yes, then it's <i>probably</i> a native Charm*; if no, it's an Evocation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> _______________<br /> *Exceptions can exist, though none have presently been written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T07:32:07-08:00","id":1282635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1282619#post1282619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One factor to keep in mind with regard to the question of whether a particular effect should be a Charm or an Evocation is, &quot;does it make sense for the Exalt to be using it <i>without</i> the Artifact?&quot; <br /> <br /> If yes, then it's <i>probably</i> a native Charm*; if no, it's an Evocation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> _______________<br /> *Exceptions can exist, though none have presently been written.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this might be the best explaination of evocations I\u2019ve seen.<br /> <br /> Somethings else that I might add though are that evocations tend to be very closely tied to a theme, and very self contained and specialized, where a lot of native charms are very general. Like take Volcano Cutter and it\u2019s crazy volcano seeding suite, for instance. <br /> <br /> Also it seems obvious but a lot of the power of evocations is focused on the weapon itself and its legend. Like an oricalcum grimcleaver might have the amazing ability to store a miniature sun within it, and have the power with its final evocation to fully open it up and release it into the sky. Throwing a new sun into the sky temporarily isn\u2019t really an extension of solar themes of human excellence, and stretches a bit far on their themes of sun-fire, but either way you wouldn\u2019t have a charm that lets you store a sun in your axe without that axe being very special itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 01-25-2019, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T08:25:15-08:00","id":1282647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1282607#post1282607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Resonant effects are supposed to be close to solar tier,</div> </div> </div> </div>How close?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T08:50:02-08:00","id":1282655,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure, but I'd like to know, for balancing purposes.<br /> <br /> Has anyone done a comparison of the more straightforward evocations and similar Solar charms?<br /> <br /> My Godspeed Vanguard's evocations seemed pretty powerful, but they were upgrades to Solar charms or combo'd with them anyway, and it was an Orichalcum Level 4 artefact.<br /> (It <i>might</i> be that Resonant evocations on Orichalcum artefacts are roughly level with Solar charms, while Jade ones are a bit weaker. They're still good for DBs because they're better than DB charms, and good for Solars because they let them do things outside the normal Solar powerset, giving them more options. I don't know though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T09:24:44-08:00","id":1282659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1282619#post1282619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One factor to keep in mind with regard to the question of whether a particular effect should be a Charm or an Evocation is, &quot;does it make sense for the Exalt to be using it <i>without</i> the Artifact?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Like my concept for the moonsilver Blood-Binding Ring.<br /> <br /> Lunars will now have multiple methods of taking Heart's Blood from people without killing them, but their ability to leverage Heart's Blood against a living victim through Lunar Charms should be limited so that a Lunar character cannot Uncontestably Win Forever against a player character whose Heart's Blood she managed to steal.<br /> <br /> But a ring can be lost, stolen, or destroyed as Lunar Charms cannot be, so an artifact ring can be allowed to give the Lunar additional power over her victims than her own Charms should ever be allowed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Kirke's Staff. Elder Lunar Exalted will have the power to transform others into beasts, but Kirke's Staff -- as something which can be lost, stolen, or destroyed -- justifies having an easier time of literally beating someone into a new shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T10:15:22-08:00","id":1282668,"title":"","content":"Yes, but ...has anyone here really ever taken an artifact away from a player? Like, for good? If so, how much whining was there afterwards?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T10:33:14-08:00","id":1282673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1282655#post1282655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(It <i>might</i> be that Resonant evocations on Orichalcum artefacts are roughly level with Solar charms, while Jade ones are a bit weaker. They're still good for DBs because they're better than DB charms, and good for Solars because they let them do things outside the normal Solar powerset, giving them more options. I don't know though.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Doubtful. The choice of magic material doesn't pose a hard limitation on what an item can do, you can have an orichalcum reaper daiklave that creates storms because it's got an imprisoned storm demon. Nothing good comes from allowing people to make a better Volcano Cutter out of orichalcum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T11:02:48-08:00","id":1282680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1282655#post1282655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone done a comparison of the more straightforward evocations and similar Solar charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's also worth comparing Evocations in Arms of the Chosen to ones in What Fire Has Wrought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T11:53:13-08:00","id":1282689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1282668#post1282668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but ...has anyone here really ever taken an artifact away from a player? Like, for good? If so, how much whining was there afterwards?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1282659#post1282659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars will now have multiple methods of taking Heart's Blood from people without killing them, but their ability to leverage Heart's Blood against a living victim through Lunar Charms should be limited so that a Lunar character cannot Uncontestably Win Forever <b>against a player character</b> whose Heart's Blood she managed to steal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about artifacts being used <i>against </i>PCs, not <i>by</i> PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T11:55:32-08:00","id":1282691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1282655#post1282655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(It <i>might</i> be that Resonant evocations on Orichalcum artefacts are roughly level with Solar charms, while Jade ones are a bit weaker. They're still good for DBs because they're better than DB charms, and good for Solars because they let them do things outside the normal Solar powerset, giving them more options. I don't know though.)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1282673#post1282673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doubtful. The choice of magic material doesn't pose a hard limitation on what an item can do, you can have an orichalcum reaper daiklave that creates storms because it's got an imprisoned storm demon. Nothing good comes from allowing people to make a better Volcano Cutter out of orichalcum.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that there's a difference between Evocations with Resonant effects, and Evocations locked behind Solar Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T10:19:58-08:00","id":1282866,"title":"","content":"Speaking more generally on the topic. The magic material is one aspect of an item's Evocations and it's shape and story might ultimately prove bigger factors.<br /> <br /> Personally speaking. I've got a system for Evocations that divides a bunch of interesting mechanical effects by appropriate weight/tags to create some initial character that I or the player can build upon.<br /> i.e. a Direlance might have initial properties derived from how long it is (Reach) its ability to puncture armour (Piercing), it's applications when used on horseback or the fact it's pretty big even for an artifact weapon (Heavy, Two-Handed).<br /> <br /> Now the magic material may already be influencing the trait I want to emphasise, the Earth themes of White Jade can work well with sheer weight. The patience associated with Earth Aspected Dragon-Blooded also compliments the Two-Handed tag. Clashes can be very powerful and worth the initiative cost of delaying your action in order to set up. Similarly a super reaching spear suggests manoeuvrability and flexibility but the idea of it literally being able to extend is Moonsilver as hell.<br /> Working with Piercing/Impaling (yeah that\u2019s a thing, core book page 203) is more material agnostic, it could be a ghostly lance tip phasing through someone\u2019s armour or rupturing their defences with a surge of essence pressure.<br /> <br /> Name is another important component of this. If I was creating a direlance on the fly for a player who didn\u2019t have any idea what they wanted their artifact to do, I\u2019d consult this random name generator <a href=\"https://www.fantasynamegenerators.com/spear-names.php\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and see what it came up with.<br /> Lightbringer<br /> King's Defender<br /> Lament<br /> Corrupted Prick<br /> Primal Harpoon<br /> Apocalyptic Yew Spike<br /> Lightning Ironbark Skewer<br /> Reign, Chopper of the Nightstalker<br /> Hail, Slayer of the Incoming Storm<br /> Wolf, Memory of Illumination<br /> <br /> A rule to keep in mind with random name generators, always Google a name before you make it a pivotal part of your character in case there\u2019s baggage associated with it that you might have missed. Suffice to say; I\u2019m not in a hurry to have one of my PCs wield the Corrupted Prick. I might have an NPC wield some tainted disease spreading direlance and add some levity to the situation by having them really not thinking their weapon name through.<br /> <br /> So let\u2019s work with Lightbringer, King\u2019s Defender and Lament.<br /> Let\u2019s play Lightbringer straight and not tie it to a certain Fallen Angel. Good for the Good God, Smite the Evildoer and all that jazz. I might say its Piercing Attack reduces a Creature of Darkness\u2019 soak by an extra -2, not huge but it it\u2019s establishing what it\u2019s here for.<br /> King\u2019s Defender is another one that\u2019s advertising its purpose. Maybe it could let the wielder Clash on behalf of another person as a sort of combined delay/defend other?<br /> Finally Lament doesn\u2019t open itself to any obvious function. The name\u2019s a bit morbid but its meaning depends on the wielder\u2019s state of mind. The name on a weapon implies regret suggesting the creator didn\u2019t want it to be wielded except in a last resort.<br /> So let\u2019s go with that. I\u2019m thinking a discount on Delaying Actions by 1, suggesting a \u201cspeak softly and carry a big stick\u201d approach that lets you measure the scene and give your allies a chance to defuse the situation before things escalate. Either because you genuinely don\u2019t want to fight or because you\u2019re the kind of assassin who doesn't want to get their clothes bloody.<br /> <br /> That's obviously not how everyone should do it, just my approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 01-26-2019, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T19:04:45-08:00","id":1282941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1282866#post1282866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suffice to say; I\u2019m not in a hurry to have one of my PCs wield the Corrupted Prick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn\u2019t that exactly what Shockwave Technique is for though? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T19:08:19-08:00","id":1282942,"title":"","content":"I thought about Primal Harpoon.<br /> <br /> Initially I thought that a longfang would be more appropriate for its role than a direlance given how harpoons are generally used, but then it occurred to me that something called Primal Harpoon might be monstrously large and more suited to the direlance statline. I imagine it as a moonsilver weapon in so far as it's an enormous piece of carved behemoth bone adorned with moonsilver telling the tale of its original wielder's victory over the monster. Its passive power is simply that it's a direlance that can be thrown up to short range but later Evocations will continue to develop it along those lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T02:42:40-08:00","id":1282993,"title":"","content":"Think of it as each source of theme or resonance for an artifact is an axis. That means you can sort times one theme with another rather then just have one theme plus another. So say you have an Orichalcum Shield. It\u2019s Orichalcum aspect could represent grandeur, heat and overwhelming force, this is one axis, it was forged in the Fires of a erupting Volcano erased from Destiny this Volcanic Expression is another Axis, and it was created in the shape of a shield and was used to save an Island from a Falling Star this is another Axis. So now you can have the grandeur axis bolster the Volcanic Expression axis to say have an evocation that gathers fulminating energy from successful defenses and having it erupt into burning magma when you wish to spend this energy. And another Evocation could use the Shield/Defender aspect combined with the burning nature axis and the infinite power aspect of Orichalcum to allow an Evocation that can nullify an overwhelming force of nature with a burning force of a Volcanoe, so say you erupt to nullify an Avalanche, or evaporate a flood, and if it saves a group or actual city or population center you call upon the savior aspect so you gain willpower, inspire hope and or get a social bonus to those you save. Thus these Evocations allow a Solar to perform miracles more in the style of mixing Dragonblooded Themes with Solar level Omnipotence, with Odd sidereal or other aftereffects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T03:42:38-08:00","id":1283006,"title":"","content":"Evocations feel to me like they should be big, flashy, specialised, high commitment (and thereby high risk, high reward). Where Charms are a slow pressure of synergising, almost always applicable utility that builds up to high strength and as aren't strongly attached to a particular image. (Contrasts even within a level of essence)<br /> <br /> Particular strengths at large scale, diffuse effects that Melee specialists in particular are relatively bad at (being better through Charms at concentrated attacks). <br /> <br /> Also relatively external and literal - you can throw a fireball at someone, you can't really push fire essence intermally through your form to enhance your skills.<br /> <br /> Ideally strongly thematically bound by the artefact beyond simple elemental / incarnal themes - the artefact is hungry, it's sad, it's resonant in song, and so on.<br /> <br /> (I now await the better and succinct quoting of what evocations can actually do from AotC that says the above better and more too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T06:23:17-08:00","id":1283028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283006#post1283006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I now await the better and succinct quoting of what evocations can actually do from AotC that says the above better and more too).</div> </div> </div> </div>You wouldn't get it, because it's not really correct; there are Evocations that are subtle, low key and internal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T08:52:58-08:00","id":1283061,"title":"","content":"Well, on a gameplay perspective, evocations should be stronger than Charms, even Solar ones.<br /> <br /> Evocations are always not favored, so they cost more, and they represent an investment on something that can be lost, and represent an opportunity cost. Suppose you get an Artifact 3, let's say its name is Grasscutter, and you buy all its evocations, and then you get Volcano Cutter, that has deeper Evocations and is *cooler* than what you've got. You have a very difficult choice of wasting the experience you spent on Grasscutter or not using Volcano Cutter.<br /> <br /> For these costs and risk, Evocations should damn right be worth it, as compared to Charms. So, they should do more, even if not by too much (or else there would be Evocation Exalted, not Solar Exalted).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","user":"pcontop","date":". 01-27-2019, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T09:16:05-08:00","id":1283064,"title":"","content":"I see your point, but being able to do a wider range of things is itself an advantage. Thus, a Solar who buys a black jade crossbow that can blow up ships and create whirlpools is getting a big advantage over his native charms; she can blow up ships and create whirlpools. That's not something she'd normally be able to do.<br /> <br /> Now, for a lot of campaigns this isn't that important. Those, of course, are the campaigns where no-one buys that Evocation tree.<br /> <br /> But in the campaign where there's loads of naval battles, where the Archery-Supernal Dawn is finding that sniping captains is useful, but not that useful because they get replaced by their subordinates, that Evocation tree is really useful, and worth the 10xp per evocation over 8xp per charm for more Archery charms; not being able to create Whirlpools is, after all, a built-in weakness of Solars that you've just found a way around.<br /> <br /> So the designer doesn't really have to think &quot;these charms for (doing something Solars can't do) need to be more powerful than Solar charms.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, this doesn't apply to low-level evocations that do stuff like add dice to damage or Parry or something, which all the splats have some equivalent of themselves. In that case, I can say that you may want them to be marginally better.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T10:37:27-08:00","id":1283076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283061#post1283061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, on a gameplay perspective, evocations should be stronger than Charms, even Solar ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Artifacts of all levels?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evocations are always not favored, so they cost more</div> </div> </div> </div>A significant number cost nothing at all, even before getting to the Solar Charms that can unlock them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose you get an Artifact 3, let's say its name is Grasscutter, and you buy all its evocations, and then you get Volcano Cutter, that has deeper Evocations and is *cooler* than what you've got. You have a very difficult choice of wasting the experience you spent on Grasscutter or not using Volcano Cutter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Volcano Cutter's first Evocation is free.<br /> <br /> Grasscutter sounds like a good choice to use if you're ever fighting in a place you don't want subjected to the logical consequences of something called Pyroclastic Holocaust Judgment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T15:41:18-08:00","id":1283132,"title":"","content":"Well, solar charms should be damn able to blow ships, be it with Archery or Throw Charms. Blowing things is totally on the Solar panoply. I think at the very least the whilrpool should be intereasting enough to be worth a purchase, or else a Sail Charm could do a better mechanical effect (of course, it's easy to make better evocations in this case because the Solar Sail Charms are mostly mediocre).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T16:02:47-08:00","id":1283136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283076#post1283076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For Artifacts of all levels?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Evocations on level 3 artifacts are just as expensive as Evocations from level 5 artifacts. High level artifacts should have more breath and more depth, but ideally similar essence level and depth effects should be on the level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A significant number cost nothing at all, even before getting to the Solar Charms that can unlock them. </div> </div> </div>'Significant', varying a lot on the artifact. A large quantity of artifacts have no free Evocations, other have more. My impression is that the artfacts that give free goodies tend to have weaker evocations that the ones that do not, and this is a way to 'make up' for this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Volcano Cutter's first Evocation is free.<br /> <br /> Grasscutter sounds like a good choice to use if you're ever fighting in a place you don't want subjected to the logical consequences of something called Pyroclastic Holocaust Judgment. </div> </div> </div>This is one more opportunity cost. You can think about investing evocations in both weapons, but at any give moment, you will be using either one weapon of the other. Melee Charms don't have this issue, they are always with you. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T16:18:38-08:00","id":1283139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283028#post1283028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You wouldn't get it, because it's not really correct; there are Evocations that are subtle, low key and internal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, I'm not talking about rules which every Evocation has to conform to. General trends that feel more in tune with evocations. You are seriously such a negative puppy sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T16:43:47-08:00","id":1283141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283136#post1283136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Evocations on level 3 artifacts are just as expensive as Evocations from level 5 artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to make a comparison to different kinds of Exalted.<br /> <br /> I think the number of times you've mentioned experience costs suggests that the level of significance you place on that detail is very different from mine, and my experience suggests to me that there's no broaching that topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">High level artifacts should have more breath and more depth, but ideally similar essence level and depth effects should be on the level.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean here by breadth and depth?<br /> <br /> Considering that Artifacts aren't really a hypothetical subject, what's your view of how they've actually been published up to this point?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression is that the artfacts that give free goodies tend to have weaker evocations that the ones that do not, and this is a way to 'make up' for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your impression is mistaken.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one more opportunity cost. You can think about investing evocations in both weapons, but at any give moment, you will be using either one weapon of the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is worlds away from the assertion that acquiring a new Artifact means either dropping a previous one or never using the new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T16:53:54-08:00","id":1283143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283139#post1283139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dude, I'm not talking about rules which every Evocation has to conform to. General trends that feel more in tune with evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your post didn't really give that impression, and I think emphasis should be placed on the alternatives because they have value in their own right and to sufficiently diversify the kinds of magic that Artifacts can provide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are seriously such a negative puppy sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say I'm more contrary, particularly considering that it's often in service of a more positive and diverse outlook of the game's system and setting.<br /> <br /> One of our more consistent points of disagreement is my looking at the Solars in terms of being intrinsically motivated to achieve positive outcomes in the setting, and you're going to call me negative?<br /> <br /> My comment disputing that Evocations are primarily or generally big and flashy and obvious comes from a sense that more subtle magics don't get enough love, and ought to be promoted. That and a feeling that focusing on that side of Evocations (particularly phrased in that way) sells their potential short.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T17:03:09-08:00","id":1283145,"title":"","content":"Big and Flashy is explicitly one of Orichalcum's themes. So everything else needs more room for subtle stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T13:17:41-08:00","id":1283340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283141#post1283141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to make a comparison to different kinds of Exalted.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>All we got is DBs?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283141#post1283141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the number of times you've mentioned experience costs suggests that the level of significance you place on that detail is very different from mine, and my experience suggests to me that there's no broaching that topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, I suppose. But let me ask, what else can you use, mechanics, side to represent the character investment?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283141#post1283141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean here by breadth and depth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depth: How deep on the tree you can get, and how powerful Evocations get, as you invest.<br /> Breadth: How varied the effects can get. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283141#post1283141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that Artifacts aren't really a hypothetical subject, what's your view of how they've actually been published up to this point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Extremely uneven, even more so when you take in consideration Arms of the Chosen and the Core rulebook. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283141#post1283141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is worlds away from the assertion that acquiring a new Artifact means either dropping a previous one or never using the new one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is not far from this. You cannot dual-wield both a Grand Daiklave and, well, whatever. Carrying both of them takes maintaining the commitment in both, and changing weapons take an action. It's simply not that practical. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T13:23:23-08:00","id":1283344,"title":"","content":"You can dual wield two daiklaves though, no problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T16:19:18-08:00","id":1283382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283340#post1283340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All we got is DBs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely. Their power is far lesser, but they are not compensated for this by significantly lower experience costs (or much of anything, really).<br /> <br /> As benefits for wielding a lower level Artifact go, one that stands out to me is that their powers are generally less of a hassle. The Melee Solar who wants only to give their own attacks a bit of oomph rather than developing and mastering a whole new fighting style, or has no personal use for wiping out everybody in a nearby radius (sometimes without meaning to), let alone any that are going to try talking them into something, I view them as thoroughly compensated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But let me ask, what else can you use, mechanics, side to represent the character investment?</div> </div> </div> </div>That metric for judgement means nothing to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depth: How deep on the tree you can get, and how powerful Evocations get, as you invest.<br /> Breadth: How varied the effects can get.</div> </div> </div> </div>How varied <i>can</i> the effects get before the item's aesthetic just becomes diffuse?<br /> <br /> Your definition of depth is already met, but for how I feel as though you're saying the first round of Evocations should be no stronger than with a lesser Artifact. It seems like it takes a long time to get the value out of your character creation Merit dots, or how much you needed to put into the crafting.<br /> <br /> And, speaking personally, I find it simply less interesting. I see a coherent and compelling structure in the difference between overall Evocation arrangements per Artifact level that has a lot more texture, a firmer basis for development, and more compelling drama than each level just being linearly more powerful than the last.<br /> <br /> Given the way the books have always talked about five-dot Artifacts, I get a lot more out of a sword that, from the word go, starts brewing up a massive storm that gets more fierce the more you cut people with it and explodes when you put it away if you don't take the time to discharge it at specific people, than I do from the sword that adds some wind or electricity after-effects to regular attacks that eventually gets distinctly strong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extremely uneven, even more so when you take in consideration Arms of the Chosen and the Core rulebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>The corebook ones I'll grant you, as they did seem to drop the ball a bit with that moonsilver bow and one or two of the armours, but I suspect that where you see unevenness, I see God loving glorious variety.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carrying both of them takes maintaining the commitment in both, and changing weapons take an action. It's simply not that practical. </div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one, considering how attunement has gone from taking a day to just a few seconds, you really don't need to maintain the commitment to several simultaneously. Have your squire/demon servant/primate familiar carry the extras around like they were your golf woods and irons.<br /> <br /> Two, it's not very much different than switching between Martial Arts Forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T22:57:05-08:00","id":1283451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283340#post1283340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cannot dual-wield both a Grand Daiklave and, well, whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not with <i>that</i> attitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T14:28:18-08:00","id":1283565,"title":"","content":"Now I'm envisioning someone welding a bunch of daiklaves to the head of a grand goremaul to make something like a giant morning star.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T14:47:14-08:00","id":1283570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283565#post1283565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm envisioning someone welding a bunch of daiklaves to the head of a grand goremaul to make something like a giant morning star.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a bunch of them in a row to make the edge of a giant axe.<br /> <br /> Someone call Jen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T07:19:48-08:00","id":1283711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283143#post1283143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My comment disputing that Evocations are primarily or generally big and flashy and obvious comes from a sense that more subtle magics don't get enough love, and ought to be promoted. That and a feeling that focusing on that side of Evocations (particularly phrased in that way) sells their potential short.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, requiring Evocations to be overt has the potential to undercut native charmsets in a different way when a Solar's wielding a jade daiklave that's basically their players favourite Dragon-Blooded charms on a stick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T16:21:15-08:00","id":1283818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283711#post1283711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, requiring Evocations to be overt has the potential to undercut native charmsets in a different way when a Solar's wielding a jade daiklave that's basically their players favourite Dragon-Blooded charms on a stick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have seen that exact thing, an artifact that's evocations were just part of a DB ability tree. It doesn't work well for a lot of reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T22:42:39-08:00","id":1283859,"title":"","content":"I'm still not 100% clear on why this doesn't work, except that in mixed circle games it kind of sucks for the DB/Lunar/Whatever. Like if I want a green jade powerbow that has Life Swelling Sap Strike, Arbor Sentinel Technique, Heartbeats Before Death, and Harvest of the Hunter, I don't see how that's not applicable to a powerbow's evocations. Maybe for Harvest of the Hunter you have to take a piece of plant life and slot it into the bow as you fire it or something, but you could also make it scenelong for having that restriction. Or some boots that let you do the whole Seething Dragon Footprint thing.<br /> <br /> Maybe there isn't? It would be a good way to keep people from falling behind in strength while letting them keep the cool elemental style. Especially if you pair it with a dragon style and let the artifact allow the user to enter aura or something. I don't think it's a good idea to introduce that kind of a thing into the official game, just because it makes actually playing as another splat really unappealing when you could just be a Solar who has all the coolest abilities from that splat, and any official thing is a nightmare for STs to say &quot;Not allowed' to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T02:40:35-08:00","id":1283881,"title":"","content":"Wanting to copy another Exalt's charms is something of a red flag for me. I'm sure it can be done benevolently but about 3/4 of the times I've seen it the player turned out to have some huge issue with the splat they were copying from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T07:24:12-08:00","id":1283920,"title":"","content":"Ahh yeah that makes sense as well. It also just occurred to me that somebody could go crazy with it and have armor that gave them lunar style shapeshifting, a shield that made their animal appear elemental and, I dunno, some kind of fate sword and just go around cherry picking the best strengths from every other splat and slapping them on a solar. At that point even in a pure Solar game you\u2019re going to run into issues with other players, partly because you look like a dick, and partly because a lot of those abilities cover over some of the very few things that Solars find hard to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T07:31:23-08:00","id":1283923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283881#post1283881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wanting to copy another Exalt's charms is something of a red flag for me. I'm sure it can be done benevolently but about 3/4 of the times I've seen it the player turned out to have some huge issue with the splat they were copying from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wings of the Raptor lets a Solar pretend to have wings like a Lunar using a winged Hybrid form, and it has an acceptable way of factoring Solar Athletics Charms into the flight it grants.<br /> <br /> I don't see why a green jade powerbow couldn't do the same with Wood-aspected Dragon-Blooded Archery Charms. Unlike actual Dragon-Blooded Archery Charms, it cannot produce effects appropriate to other elements for a Solar user, and it won't let a Solar gain a Wood Aura for use with Immaculate Wood Dragon Style Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is not to say that the powerbow's Evocations should be exact 1-to-1 copies of Terrestrial Archery Charms, of course, but &quot;plant the bow into the ground to become an artillery tree&quot; should be fine as an Evocaiton, and mechanically the Charms would be similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T07:35:57-08:00","id":1283925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283923#post1283923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike actual Dragon-Blooded Archery Charms, it cannot produce effects appropriate to other elements for a Solar user.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m actually not sure this is true, if it was a blue and green jade powerbow meant to evoke the feelings of being in a forest during a storm or something, it might be able to grab most of the DB charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T09:38:57-08:00","id":1283952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283925#post1283925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m actually not sure this is true, if it was a blue and green jade powerbow meant to evoke the feelings of being in a forest during a storm or something, it might be able to grab most of the DB charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how such a theme lends itself to pure-Wood effects like growing into a tree or its arrows becoming nets. Those things have nothing to do with storms regardless of location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T09:46:48-08:00","id":1283953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283952#post1283952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know how such a theme lends itself to pure-Wood effects like growing into a tree or its arrows becoming nets. Those things have nothing to do with storms regardless of location.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that\u2019s a good point.m, I\u2019m not sure if artifacts can split like that down the lines, unless the artifact in question has a theme of duality, which is hard to do because blue and green jade aren\u2019t really opposite sides of the same coin or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T18:57:32-08:00","id":1284053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1283923#post1283923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wings of the Raptor lets a Solar pretend to have wings like a Lunar using a winged Hybrid form, and it has an acceptable way of factoring Solar Athletics Charms into the flight it grants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flight has never been a Lunar niche though, it's just something they can do with very little effort.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T12:28:26-08:00","id":1284186,"title":"","content":"I can see someone going \u201cHey, these DB Archery charms are really cool, I like the plant manipulation angle, I want that for my green jade powerbow.\u201d And the ST, not being particularly skilled with homebrew, just slaps the charms on it and calls it done. I think that can work and isn\u2019t necessarily going to produce worse results than creating your own Evocations from scratch.<br /> <br /> However, I do agree with Lioness that it might come from a disingenuous angle and it can cause potential issues with splat diversity, so it is usually better to try to create your own Evocations that match the theme you want, instead of just taking a set of charms wholesale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T13:51:10-08:00","id":1284203,"title":"","content":"Copying Charms as Evocations could work if you really have trouble with homebrew, although I <i>definitely</i> wouldn't do it if you have someone else actually using the relevant Charms. If someone is already playing a Dragon-Blooded archer, you might want to come up with something else for your powerbow.<br /> <br /> ...I kinda want to see a 3e version of the Deadly Transformation Armor now. There should be a lot of cool Evocations you could develop for a transforming moonsilver armor without actually duplicating DBT. (Well, I assume anyway. I guess we don't know how 3e DBT will work yet.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T14:33:56-08:00","id":1284217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1282574-evocations-vs-charms?p=1284186#post1284186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I do agree with Lioness that it might come from a disingenuous angle and it can cause potential issues with splat diversity, so it is usually better to try to create your own Evocations that match the theme you want, instead of just taking a set of charms wholesale.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not necessarily something they're actively doing to spite you and ruin your game, but someone who wants Dragon-Blooded charms on their Solar probably has an <i>interesting</i> relationship with Dragon-Blooded that you don't want to be blindsided by.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T18:32:28-08:00","id":1284258,"title":"","content":"The bow has its appeal to the Dragon-Blooded too, since its Evocations would lack the Wood keyword and thus not interfere with Air or Water Auras.<br /> <br /> And of course, knowing the parallel Wood-Elemental Archery Charms could make the woody Evocations more powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}